{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When you come into the land.</b> To the Galilee of the nations (Torat Kohanim 2)." "<b>And the land shall rest.</b> The lands prepared for agricultural work." "<b>A sabbath unto HaShem.</b> That the entire year, desisted from agricultural work, be dedicated to His service — just as He intended regarding the Sabbath of Creation, in saying: שַׁבָּת לַה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ (Exodus 20:7)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {2 "Sforno cites Exodus 20:7 but the verse 'שַׁבָּת לַה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ' in the Decalogue is at Exodus 20:10 (20:7 in some editions is a different verse); the verse address is retained as given in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:52.127936554Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}